From 78a8cef86d6985e72f63153c36c31265490fd6e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:35:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webmock): x-gemini-api-privileged-user-id is a secret
 header; scrub what the first recordings kept

The gemini cassettes carried the Google account id behind the API key in
x-gemini-api-privileged-user-id, and the pi cassette carried the recording
machine's scratch path inside its base64 response chunks (the model echoed
its cwd). Both scrubbed: the header to <redacted>, the path to <scratch>
like the request bodies already were. The header joins SECRET_HEADERS so
the recorder never writes it again.

goldens-baseline/*/project.stderr named the capture machine's home six
times; now <repo>. Nothing hashes those files (manifest.tsv covers inputs,
IR and outputs only).
